---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Redshift Data Warehouse Modernisation | Case Study">
	<article class="case-study-page">
		<header class="cs-hero container section-padding">
			<a href="/#case-studies" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Case Studies</a>
			<span class="category">Enterprise Data Architecture</span>
			<h1 class="text-gradient">Redshift Data Warehouse Modernisation</h1>
			<p class="cs-subtitle">Establishing a single source of truth and scalable data foundations.</p>
		</header>

		<div class="cs-image-banner">
			<img src="/images/project_redshift.png" alt="Redshift Architecture" />
		</div>

		<section class="container section-padding cs-content">
			<div class="content-grid">
				<div class="main-body">
					<h2 class="gold-accent">The Challenge</h2>
					<p>
						As organizations scale, legacy data architectures often struggle to maintain quality controls and provide a unified enterprise view, leading to disparate data assets and fragmented business intelligence. The goal was to consolidate diverse data sources into a robust, centralized repository capable of supporting advanced analytics.
					</p>

					<h2 class="gold-accent">The Solution</h2>
					<p>
						I designed and implemented an enterprise-grade Redshift Data Warehouse utilizing the Kimball methodology and Medallion Architecture principles. This involved building hands-on ETL pipelines to systematically process raw data through Bronze (Raw), Silver (Operational), and Gold (Application) layers. The architecture prioritized interoperability, rigorous data quality, and transparent data lineage.
					</p>

					<h2 class="gold-accent">The Impact</h2>
					<p>
						The modernization initiative successfully established an enterprise-wide single source of truth. By automating key data pipelines and optimizing ETL/ELT processes, we significantly reduced manual overhead. The robust foundation enabled a culture of data-driven decision-making, providing downstream users with trustworthy, self-service Business Intelligence capabilities.
					</p>
				</div>
				<aside class="cs-sidebar glass">
					<h3>Technologies</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Amazon Redshift</li>
						<li>Medallion Architecture</li>
						<li>Kimball Methodology</li>
						<li>ETL / ELT Automation</li>
						<li>SQL Data Modelling</li>
					</ul>
					<h3>Role</h3>
					<p>Data Warehouse Engineer</p>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.case-study-page {
		min-height: 100vh;
	}

	.cs-hero {
		padding-bottom: 4rem;
		text-align: center;
		max-width: 900px;
	}

	.back-link {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		font-weight: 500;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}

	.back-link:hover {
		color: var(--accent-gold);
	}

	.category {
		display: block;
		color: var(--accent-gold);
		font-weight: 600;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.cs-subtitle {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	.cs-image-banner {
		width: 100%;
		max-height: 60vh;
		overflow: hidden;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
	}

	.cs-image-banner img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		display: block;
	}

	.content-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
		gap: 4rem;
	}

	.main-body h2 {
		font-size: 2rem;
		margin-top: 3rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.main-body h2:first-child {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.main-body p {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.cs-sidebar {
		padding: 2.5rem;
		border-radius: 1rem;
		height: fit-content;
		position: sticky;
		top: 120px;
	}

	.cs-sidebar h3 {
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}

	.cs-sidebar ul {
		list-style: none;
		margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
	}

	.cs-sidebar ul li {
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		padding-left: 1.5rem;
		position: relative;
	}

	.cs-sidebar ul li::before {
		content: '▹';
		color: var(--accent-gold);
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
	}

	.cs-sidebar p {
		color: var(--text-secondary);
	}

	@media (max-width: 992px) {
		.content-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.cs-sidebar {
			position: static;
		}
	}
</style>
